1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,909
Paste the week, press Read and price.

2
00:00:02,909 --> 00:00:07,820
Gemma reads it offline; the counter shows real seconds, about thirteen.

3
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:10,932
Seven shifts, ten invoice lines, three flags.

4
00:00:10,932 --> 00:00:15,567
The red one is the pantry, quoted exactly, with its notify-by date.

5
00:00:15,567 --> 00:00:18,817
The PRN and bed rails: authorised, record only.

6
00:00:18,817 --> 00:00:24,420
Then the shifts Gemma read, the lines code priced, a Why on each, and a printable

7
00:00:24,420 --> 00:00:26,080
invoice per participant.

8
00:00:26,980 --> 00:00:29,850
Same job from a photo of a paper diary.

9
00:00:29,850 --> 00:00:32,940
Drop it in, run, and the shifts come back.

10
00:00:45,976 --> 00:00:46,684
And voice.

11
00:00:46,684 --> 00:00:48,594
Three memos, one per shift.

12
00:00:48,594 --> 00:00:52,627
Gemma hears the audio directly; no separate speech model.

13
00:00:52,627 --> 00:00:57,296
What Gemma heard opens for checking; the shifts land in the table.
